#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9054393-30f1-5923-b32e-15ea3acad0ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386839} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf652d2-fa3b-5fdf-bb1d-6a8462c2431b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386840} {:answer/id #uuid "1382cad3-718b-55f0-a61e-4224134a2cd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386841} {:answer/id #uuid "1ccd5358-c0ab-5bea-b689-dc701eb72069" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386842} {:answer/id #uuid "35b83e50-5a21-54e1-931d-7091856c0a0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ccd5358-c0ab-5bea-b689-dc701eb72069" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386842} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4871325-33a7-51eb-8af2-dcd6a6b97c80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59028158-753f-502a-bd86-d054f28eae13" :question/math-academy-id "q-130922" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-3y-1,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-3y-1 \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fa24236-4a87-5b19-82dc-1b1593ea610e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386846} {:answer/id #uuid "d1edcbbb-9d9a-5ad0-bde3-3fde951d4a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386847} {:answer/id #uuid "d17a02a7-dc78-59ce-b854-4e616189baa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386848} {:answer/id #uuid "f677cbb4-ef6d-5c06-b7e8-343fba1061ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386849} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebc0ac4-f033-51b8-9432-f4e3f0ff5e56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d17a02a7-dc78-59ce-b854-4e616189baa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386848} :answer-field/id #uuid "639420bc-b662-5eef-8212-3d10fa1e9bbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "653d2739-ff74-51ff-bc93-114e79b1a15b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42153" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 3x+9y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106241 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11c48728-7b02-57ec-ba2b-49ae0c32c250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386852} {:answer/id #uuid "0500f257-a8cd-568a-9bc4-5657a1262a10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386853} {:answer/id #uuid "f44fbff9-976f-5fcc-8423-4607a07508e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386854} {:answer/id #uuid "54704bdc-c31c-59d0-b581-56b96711eb09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386855} {:answer/id #uuid "63c74d62-cd4c-5afe-84e2-57a8b7aced67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54704bdc-c31c-59d0-b581-56b96711eb09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386855} :answer-field/id #uuid "36f5e20a-48c7-5cad-8cfd-89381794a4ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6118a9d-772a-5b19-befb-3156e01fd7c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42155" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=3 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-y=3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3+y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3+y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71985084-024d-5240-8df3-c775e8ff5571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386859} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa1ce79-3c94-5097-8c92-c5a09759b978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386860} {:answer/id #uuid "4e61db4d-def4-5548-80af-8e2f6152eb51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386861} {:answer/id #uuid "690d484c-33f3-5456-bbd8-4cedbabc9223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386862} {:answer/id #uuid "137e4fc9-3cf1-5aad-abee-06f6bea29842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71985084-024d-5240-8df3-c775e8ff5571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386859} :answer-field/id #uuid "599d4de6-db25-5015-aab3-2ab595339a3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e4d5c647-074f-5eda-b4fd-fd73311149f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-73751" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-10y=-5 \\\\ 2x-4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=4$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=4,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "297f7331-aac8-553f-ba85-90bbc635da4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323250} {:answer/id #uuid "d42041b6-0d0c-57c1-ba96-f611b56a3888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323251} {:answer/id #uuid "5b83f105-9641-50d2-945e-0ab8ddd3b95f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323252} {:answer/id #uuid "d39b1fc1-0fd1-5571-a534-24778b8b105a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323253} {:answer/id #uuid "5a94be43-fac2-5b10-8bc0-57ff3e4cbd7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b83f105-9641-50d2-945e-0ab8ddd3b95f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323252} :answer-field/id #uuid "06d8610c-28df-5a5f-b83b-554ec39b63ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e91f6a97-d964-5da3-939c-23c41ba726cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-73752" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-6y=10 \\\\ -x+3y=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=5 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=5.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=5+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
